## Why This Is Asked
This problem tests understanding of partition dynamic programming with nontrivial segment costs, requiring careful recurrence formulation, efficient range query handling, and solution reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- Partition DP with fixed number of contiguous segments
- Segment cost computation using range max-min queries
- Reconstruction via predecessor pointers
- Time/space optimization techniques

## Code Example
```javascript
function minCostPartitions(A, k) {
  const n = A.length;
  const dp = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => Array(k + 1).fill(Infinity));
  const pre = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => Array(k + 1).fill(-1));

  dp[0][0] = 0;

  // Base case: single segment
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    let maxVal = A[0], minVal = A[0];
    for (let j = 0; j < i; j++) {
      maxVal = Math.max(maxVal, A[j]);
      minVal = Math.min(minVal, A[j]);
      dp[i][1] = maxVal - minVal;
    }
  }

  // DP transitions
  for (let t = 2; t <= k; t++) {
    for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
      for (let j = t - 1; j < i; j++) {
        const segmentCost = computeCost(A, j + 1, i);
        if (dp[j][t - 1] + segmentCost < dp[i][t]) {
          dp[i][t] = dp[j][t - 1] + segmentCost;
          pre[i][t] = j;
        }
      }
    }
  }

  // Reconstruct segments
  const segments = [];
  let end = n;
  for (let t = k; t >= 1; t--) {
    const start = pre[end][t] + 1;
    segments.unshift([start, end]);
    end = pre[end][t];
  }

  return { minCost: dp[n][k], segments };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests a fresh DP angle: combine subproblem best within intervals with partition into exactly k blocks, ensuring non-overlap and order.

## Key Concepts

- Precompute bestSubarray(l, r) for all intervals.
- Knapsack-style DP over blocks: dp[i][t] = max over l of dp[l-1][t-1] + bestSubarray(l, i).
- Reconstruction: store the chosen l for each dp[i][t].
- Complexity: O(n^2 k) time, O(n^2) for bestSubarray and O(nk) for DP.

## Code Example

```javascript
function solve(A, k) {
  const n = A.length;
  // 1) bestSubarray(l, r)
  const best = Array.from({ length: n }, () => Array(n).fill(-Infinity));
  for (let l = 0; l < n; l++) {
    let maxEnding = 0;
    let bestSoFar = -Infinity;
    for (let r = l; r < n; r++) {
      maxEnding = Math.max(A[r], maxEnding + A[r]);
      bestSoFar = Math.max(bestSoFar, maxEnding);
      best[l][r] = bestSoFar;
    }
  }
  // 2) DP over i, t
  const dp = Array.from({ length: n }, () => Array(k + 1).fill(-Infinity));
  const par = Array.from({ length: n }, () => Array(k + 1).fill(-1));
  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) dp[i][1] = best[0][i], par[i][1] = -2;
  for (let t = 2; t <= k; t++) {
    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
      let bestVal = -Infinity, bestL = -1;
      for (let l = t - 1; l <= i; l++) {
        const cand = (l - 1 >= 0 ? dp[l - 1][t - 1] : 0) + best[l][i];
        if (cand > bestVal) { bestVal = cand; bestL = l; }
      }
      dp[i][t] = bestVal;
      par[i][t] = bestL;
    }
  }
  // reconstruction omitted for brevity
  return { bestValue: dp[n - 1][k], blocks: [] };
}
```

